Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 02:17:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/20] B1-3 (H-4): import FAILED into shell server; add
 start-worker failure regression
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

server.py imported ModuleRunner, EXTERNAL, READY, DEGRADED, STARTING but not FAILED while _start_worker's except path used it: a runner whose start() raised produced a secondary NameError instead of FAILED(PROCESS_START_FAILED), leaving the runner stuck in STARTING. One-line import fix; no behavior change on any non-failing path.

Regression: shell/tests/test_start_worker_failure.py — FAILED constant present; raising start() records FAILED/PROCESS_START_FAILED (no NameError); real ModuleRunner failing before CreateProcessW ends FAILED with zero spawn attempts (no orphan). Fail-before: 1 failure + 2 errors incl. 'NameError: name FAILED is not defined'; pass-after 3/3 OK.

shell/BUILD-MANIFEST.txt regenerated by the shell suite's own manifest machinery: entries 62 -> 63, the delta being the new test file (kept so the ledger matches the tree).

Directive SWS-REM-DIR-20260828 R2 BATCH 1 item B1-3. Seat: builder qwen3.8-max. UTC: 2026-08-28T02:17:03+00:00
